 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys
+
+Sign-in, sign-up, and account settings (`/account`) support passkeys (WebAuthn):
+
+- **Sign up**: after creating an account, users are offered a passkey (platform authenticator).
+- **Sign in**: passkeys appear in the username field's autofill (conditional mediation) and via a
+  "Sign in with a passkey" button. After a password sign-in, the browser may silently upgrade to a
+  passkey (conditional create); otherwise a passkey prompt is shown.
+- **Account settings**: list, rename, remove, and create passkeys (security keys allowed), and edit
+  the display name. Password managers are kept in sync with the WebAuthn Signal API.
+- **Reauthentication**: adding/removing passkeys and changing account details require a sign-in
+  within the last 5 minutes; otherwise users confirm with one of their passkeys (or their password).
+
+Password sign-in/sign-up are proxied through `/api/auth/*` to the existing account service so the
+server can hold a session. Passkey data is stored in a JSON file. Server-side verification uses
+[SimpleWebAuthn](https://github.com/MasterKale/SimpleWebAuthn).
+
+| Variable           | Default                     | Purpose                                                    |
+| ------------------ | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `WEBAUTHN_RP_ID`   | request hostname            | Relying Party ID (e.g. `astro-news-pytrpecapa-uc.a.run.app`) |
+| `WEBAUTHN_ORIGINS` | request origin              | Comma-separated allowed origins                            |
+| `AUTH_DB_PATH`     | `.data/auth-db.json`        | Passkey/account store (use a persistent volume in prod)    |
+
+Passkeys require a secure context: `https://` or `http://localhost`.
