+
+## Accounts & passkeys
+
+Usernames and passwords are verified by the upstream Times auth service, proxied through
+`/api/auth/login` and `/api/auth/register` so the app can keep a server-side session.
+Passkeys (WebAuthn, via [SimpleWebAuthn](https://simplewebauthn.dev/)) are layered on top:
+
+- **Sign in** (`/signin`): passkeys are offered in the username field's autofill (conditional
+  mediation), plus a "Sign in with a passkey" button. After a password sign-in, browsers that
+  support it silently upgrade the account with a passkey (conditional create); otherwise the
+  user is invited to create one.
+- **Sign up** (`/signup`): new accounts are signed in and prompted to create a passkey.
+- **Account settings** (`/account`): list, create, rename and remove passkeys. Adding or
+  removing a passkey requires a recent sign-in; otherwise the user is asked to confirm it's
+  them with a passkey or their password. The WebAuthn Signal API keeps password managers in
+  sync with removed passkeys and username changes.
+
+Passkey credentials are stored in a JSON file (`.data/passkeys.json` by default). Configure with:
+
+| Variable             | Default                     | Purpose                                        |
+| -------------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
+| `PASSKEY_STORE_PATH` | `./.data/passkeys.json`     | Location of the credential store               |
+| `PASSKEY_RP_ID`      | request hostname            | WebAuthn relying party ID                      |
+| `PASSKEY_ORIGINS`    | request origin              | Comma-separated list of allowed origins        |
+
+Passkeys require a secure context (HTTPS or `localhost`).
