--- /dev/null
+++ b/PRIVACY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+# Privacy by Design — The Daily Grind website
+
+Engineering reference for how the site protects visitor privacy. The public-facing
+policy lives at `/privacy-policy`; a short summary is in the page footer under
+"Your privacy at a glance".
+
+## Principles
+
+1. **Data minimization**: if we don't collect it, it can't leak. No analytics,
+   no tracking pixels, no fingerprinting, nothing kept in Web Storage.
+2. **Private by default**: there are no tracking cookies, so there is no consent
+   banner and nothing for visitors to opt out of.
+3. **Purpose limitation**: account data is used only for orders and rewards, never
+   repurposed (for example, for marketing) without fresh, explicit consent.
+4. **Transparency and control**: the footer explains what we do in plain language
+   and links to self-service export, correction, and deletion.
+
+## Third-party audit
+
+| Date       | Resource                                        | Purpose    | Data exposed to third party        | Decision |
+|------------|-------------------------------------------------|------------|------------------------------------|----------|
+| 2026-11-15 | `images.unsplash.com` hero background (hotlink) | Hero image | Visitor IP, User-Agent, Referer, timing on every page view | **Removed.** Image downloaded once, EXIF stripped, served from `/assets/img/` (JPEG + WebP). |
+
+**Current third parties: none.** Every request the homepage makes goes to our own origin.
+`Content-Security-Policy` and `Connection-Allowlist` enforce this, so a stray third
+party breaks loudly instead of leaking quietly.
+
+### Before adding a third party
+
+- Prove it's needed and that a first-party or static option won't do (for example,
+  plain share links instead of social SDKs).
+- Record a HAR file / DevTools network log: what is sent, to whom, and which
+  cookies are set.
+- Prefer privacy modes (`youtube-nocookie.com`) and the façade pattern: show a
+  static placeholder and load the embed only when the visitor clicks.
+- Pin versioned URLs and add `integrity` + `crossorigin="anonymous"` +
+  `referrerpolicy="no-referrer"`.
+- Never load it on account, rewards, or checkout pages.
+- Add the origin to the specific CSP directive and `Connection-Allowlist` (in both
+  `_headers` and the `<meta>` CSP in `index.html`), then add a row to the table above.
+
+## Client-side data handling (`assets/js/privacy.js`)
+
+- **Tracking parameter stripping**: `utm_*`, `gclid`, `fbclid`, `msclkid`, and
+  similar parameters are removed from the URL with `history.replaceState`, so they
+  aren't kept in history or bookmarks or passed on when visitors share links.
+- **Storage allowlist**: `ALLOWED_STORAGE_KEYS` is empty. Any `localStorage` or
+  `sessionStorage` entry not on that list is deleted on load. Never store tokens or
+  PII there, because any script on the origin can read it.
+- **Logout**: the logout control is a `POST` form (prefetchers, crawlers, and
+  cross-site links can't trigger it). The client clears all Web Storage on submit,
+  and the server response sends `Clear-Site-Data: "cookies", "storage"`.
+- **Global Privacy Control**: when `navigator.globalPrivacyControl` is true, the
+  footer tells the visitor that the signal was received and honored.
+- **No fingerprinting**: feature detection only. No UA sniffing, canvas, font, or
+  device enumeration.
+
+## Response headers (`_headers`)
+
+| Header | Why |
+|---|---|
+| `Content-Security-Policy` | `default-src 'none'` with only `'self'` sources: no third-party scripts, styles, images, frames, or beacons. `form-action 'self'` stops forms from posting data elsewhere. Trusted Types are enforced. No `'unsafe-inline'`, because all CSS and JS are external files. |
+| `Connection-Allowlist` | Same-origin-only network allowlist that also covers channels CSP doesn't (preconnect, DNS prefetch, WebRTC). `redirects=allow` lets same-origin redirects through (for example, after logout). |
+| `Reporting-Endpoints` | Violation reports go to our own endpoint. Reports contain URLs, so the endpoint must scrub query strings and must not log IPs. |
+| `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin` | Cross-origin requests get the origin only, never paths or query strings. |
+| `Permissions-Policy` | Turns off powerful and advertising APIs (camera, mic, geolocation, Topics, Protected Audience, Attribution Reporting, Shared Storage, …) for us and anything we might embed. |
+| `Clear-Site-Data` (on `/logout`) | Removes cookies and storage from the browser at sign-out. |
+| `Cache-Control: no-store` (account, rewards, orders) | Personal pages are never kept in shared or back/forward caches. |
+| `X-Robots-Tag: noindex` (account, rewards) | Keeps personal pages out of search engines. |
+| HSTS, `nosniff`, `X-Frame-Options`, COOP/CORP, `Origin-Agent-Cluster` | Transport and isolation hardening that privacy depends on. |
+
+The local `pnpm start` server (statikk) does not apply `_headers`. Locally, only the
+`<meta>` CSP and referrer policy are active. Production hosting must serve `_headers`
+(Netlify and Cloudflare Pages do this natively; other hosts need equivalent config).
+
+## Server-side requirements (outside this repo)
+
+- Session cookie: `Set-Cookie: __Host-session=…; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Path=/`.
+  This is the only cookie, and it's set only after sign-in.
+- `/logout` accepts `POST` only and sends the `_headers` response headers.
+- `/account/data-export`, `/account/profile`, and `/account/delete` give
+  self-service access, correction, and erasure.
+- Mask emails, tokens, and IDs in logs. Rate-limit account and lookup endpoints.
+- Delete order and contact data once its purpose and legal retention period end.
